{"id":"2023-505214-23-00","src":"ctis","title":"PRODIGE 87 FOXTROT II : Personalising and refining neo-adjuvant chemotherapy in locally advanced but resectable colon cancer in the elderly of 70 years old or more","official":"PRODIGE 87 FOXTROT II : Personalising and refining neo-adjuvant chemotherapy in locally advanced but resectable colon cancer in the elderly of 70 years old or more","summary":"Main objective: The primary objective is to demonstrate that the proportion of patients alive and disease-free at  3 years after randomization treated with 6 weeks (3 courses) of NeoAdjuvant Chemotherapy (FOLFOX) followed by surgery is superior compared to those going Straight To Surgery.","conditions":["colon carcinoma","Adenocarcinoma of colon"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"FOLINIC ACID"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"FLUOROURACIL"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"OXALIPLATIN"}],"criteria":"Inclusion criteria:\n1. Biopsy-confirmed adenocarcinoma of the colon, high-grade dysplasia is acceptable with unequivocal radiological evidence of invasive cancer\n2. Adequate renal biochemistry\n3. Adequate hepatobiliary function\n4. Patient able to understand and willing to provide written informed consent for the study\n5. Patient affiliated to a social security scheme\n6. Radiological stage T3/T4 and N0/N1/N2 and M0\n7. Patient eligible for curative surgery\n8. No clinical or radiological evidence of bowel obstruction\n9. Age ≥ 70 at the time of registration\n10. pMMR/MSS tumour status\n11. Colon cancer specialist assessed fit to receive 6 weeks (3 courses) of NAC with FOLFOX and surgery\n12. Homozygous for DPYD germline mutation\n13. Homozygous for DPYD germline mutation\nExclusion criteria:\n1. Any patient for whom radiotherapy is advised by the multidisciplinary team metting\n2. Person under guardianship, curatorship, and safeguard of justice or person deprived of liberty\n3. Impossible to undergo the medical follow-up of the trial for geographical, social or psychological reasons\n4. Hypersensitivity to the active substance of the trial treatments or to any of the excipients\n5. Patient with poor nutritional status at appreciation by each clinician\n6. bone marrow hypoplasia\n7. Potentially severe infection 1 month before NAC\n8. Patients who have received live attenuated vaccines (yellow fever, varicella, shingles, measles, mumps, rubella, tuberculosis, rotavirus, influenza) 1 month before NAC\n9. Any chronic condition not balanced in the last 6 months: liver failure, renal failure, respiratory failure, heart failu\n10. QT/QTc interval > 450 msec for men and > 470 msec for women\n11. Known Pernicious anaemia or other anaemias due to vitamin B12 deficiency\n12. Strong evidence of distant metastases or peritoneal nodules\n13. Peritonitis\n14. T1-T2\n15. Serious medical comorbidity, as assessed by leading clinician\n16. Any other malignant disease within the preceding 5 years with the exception of non-melanomatous skin cancer, carcinoma in situ and early stage disease with a recurrence risk <10%\n17. Known dMMR/ MSI-H tumour status\n18. Have a peripheral sensitive neuropathy with functional impairment\n19. Recent (within four weeks prior to randomisation) or concomitant treatment with brivudine, sorivudine or their chemically related analogues","minAge":"65 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"","enrollment":null,"start":"2024-06-07","pcd":"2031-09-01","upd":"2026-11-24","sponsor":"Centre Hospitalier Universitaire De Dijon","areas":["oncology"],"central":["coordinator · 0555055555 · niki.christou@chu-limoges.fr"],"sites":[{"f":"GHBS Lorient – Digestive Oncology","city":"Lorient","zip":"","c":"Caroline COUFFON · 0297067455 · c.couffon@ghbs.bzh","s":"R","pr":"","lat":47.7482,"lon":-3.3718},{"f":"CHU Rennes Pontchaillou Hospital – Oncology","city":"Rennes","zip":"35033","c":"Corentin DUPUIS · 0299283282 · corentin.dupuis@chu-rennes.fr","s":"R","pr":"","lat":48.1111,"lon":-1.6743},{"f":"Centre Hospi